HINT NOTREADY: kubelet is not posting Ready: oc describe node, oc adm node-logs NODE -u kubelet; pods are evicted after the unreachable toleration (300s)
HINT MEMORYPRESSURE: memory.available is under the eviction threshold: find the top consumers (oc adm top pods), fix requests/limits, check kubelet systemReserved
HINT DISKPRESSURE: nodefs/imagefs is low: crictl images / du on /var/lib/containers, rotate logs, check ephemeral-storage requests
HINT PIDPRESSURE: pid.available is low: find a fork bomb or leaking process (ps -eLf), raise podPidsLimit only after you know why
HINT NOTAINT: pressure is True but the node.kubernetes.io/*-pressure taint is missing: the scheduler may still place pods here
HINT EVICTIONSTORM: 5+ evictions on one node: the pressure is chronic; cordon, drain and fix the cause before it takes the node down
HINT EVICTIONS: kubelet evicted pods here: the pressure came and went; compare victims' usage with their requests (BestEffort/Burstable go first)
